{"id":3761,"date":"2021-09-24T09:31:50","date_gmt":"2021-09-24T16:31:50","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3761"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:35:41","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:35:41","slug":"3-5-random","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/3-5-random\/","title":{"rendered":"3.5: Random"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfaf5\" name=\"6a22149dbfaf5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Goals and Steps to Success<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Goals:<\/p>\n<p>By the end of this lesson, I will be able to:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Describe how a computer generates random numbers<\/li>\n<li>Describe the range of numbers generated by default from a random number generator<\/li>\n<li>Explain how to convert random numbers into useable ranges of values in a pogram<\/li>\n<li>Explain how random numbers can be valuable in a program<\/li>\n<li>Write a program that uses random numbers to impact drone flight<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Steps to Success:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Random Function<\/li>\n<li>Random LED<\/li>\n<li>Random Practice Exercises<\/li>\n<li>Random Flight Path<\/li>\n<li>Number Guessing Program<\/li>\n<li>Challenge 1: Magic 8 Ball<\/li>\n<li>Challenge 2: Random Flight<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfccd\" name=\"6a22149dbfccd\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Random Function<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The\u00a0<em><strong>random<\/strong><\/em><em>\u00a0<\/em>library in python allows use to generate a variety of random numbers. To learn more about the random library and its functions, click <a href=\"https:\/\/docs.python.org\/3\/library\/random.html\">HERE<\/a> to go to the official documentation. In the following video, we explore how random numbers work in python. Make sure you create a new file in your Level 3 Directory called\u00a0<em>random_practice<\/em> before getting started:<\/p>\n<div style=\"width: 1200px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-3761-1\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video\/mp4\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/random-intro.mp4?_=1\" \/><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/random-intro.mp4\">https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/random-intro.mp4<\/a><\/video><\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfd62\" name=\"6a22149dbfd62\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Random LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">One of the ways you can see return values with your CoDrone Mini is through its LED and number randomization. Quick review from the LED lesson: <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">an LED produces color as a combination of red, green, and blue. All of these values range from 0 to 255 corresponding to the color&#8217;s intensity, with 255 being the highest.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">For this program, import the CoDrone Mini, time, and random libraries, and then create the drone object and pair to CoDrone Mini. Next, create a for loop that will run three times.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">In the loop, create variables that will get a random number between 0 and 255 for red, blue, and green. Those three numbers are combined together to change the LED\u2019s color. For example, if your program returned RGB values of 13, 246, and 197, your CoDrone Mini\u2019s LED would turn aqua.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Next, have your drone take off, wait briefly, and then return the red, green, and blue random numbers with a brightness of 100. This should change the color of your drone\u2019s LED. After that, have the drone land.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Try this program out, and once you see what happens, once you get it working, try to add a random value for brightness as well!<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nimport time\r\n\r\nfrom random import randint\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\n\r\nfor i in range(3):\r\n\r\n    red = randint(0,255)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 blue = randint(0,255)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 green = randint(0,255)\r\n\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.takeoff()\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 time.sleep(0.05)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.LED_color(red,blue,green, 100)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.land()\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfdce\" name=\"6a22149dbfdce\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Random Practice Exercises<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To practice our knowledge with the different random functions, try writing programs that do the following:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Print a random value between 100 and 1000<\/li>\n<li>Select a random color from a list of 5 colors of your choosing<\/li>\n<li>Print a random decimal value between 0 and 1<\/li>\n<li>Select a random flight sequence from a list of sequences and have the drone fly the sequence<\/li>\n<li>Select a random color sequence from a list of sequences and have the drone play it<\/li>\n<li>CHALLENGE: Print a random value between 10 and 20 WITHOUT using the randint(a,b) function<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Now try to create a program that selects a random integer for a move() function and a random integer for a flight direction function (pitch, yaw, roll, or throttle). Have the drone take off and fly the direction and duration based on the two random values you generated.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfe3e\" name=\"6a22149dbfe3e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Random Flight Path<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this activity, we are going to create a list of flight directions AND random numbers and see where our drone goes! To do this, create a new file in your Level 3 directory called\u00a0<em>random_flight.\u00a0<\/em>Now import CoDrone mini and random, create your drone and pair it.<\/p>\n<p>We are now going to create 3 variables. One is a list of flight directions, the others are the power and duration for that movement:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">directions = [\"yaw\", \"pitch\", \"roll\", \"throttle\"] #different flight path options\r\nduration = random.randint(1,5) # 1 to 5 seconds for our movement\r\npower = random.randint(20,100) # Random power value that starts at 20 so we at least see some movement<\/pre>\n<p>Now that we have these created, let&#8217;s make our movement based off of the random values:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">drone.takeoff()\r\nrand_dir = random.choice(directions)\r\nif rand_dir == \"yaw\":\r\n    drone.set_yaw(power)\r\nelif rand_dir == \"pitch\":\r\n    drone.set_pitch(power)\r\nelif rand_dir == \"pitch\":\r\n    drone.set_roll(power)\r\nelif rand_dir == \"throttle\":\r\n    drone.set_throttle(power)<\/pre>\n<p>Finally, add the move, land, and close commands:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">drone.move(duration)\r\n\r\ndrone.land()\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>Try out the program and see how it works! Once you have it running, can you think of any other additions or optimizations you could make to the code?[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbfeb4\" name=\"6a22149dbfeb4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Number Guessing Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">You know that game that starts with \u201cI\u2019m thinking of a number\u2026\u201d and you have to guess which number the person is thinking of? You\u2019re going to play that with your drone!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">After importing libraries (CoDrone, direction, time, and random), creating the drone object, and pairing, have your drone take off. Next, create a variable called \u00a0<code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">throttle<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">and set its value to 20.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Create a variable called \u00a0<code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">number<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">that will store and return a number between 1 and 10. Next, create a while loop. Create a variable called \u00a0<code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">guess<\/code>\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">that will prompt the user to input a number between 1 and 10, and will then store that value. Within the while loop, set up conditionals. If their guess is too low, the drone should throttle down. If their guess is too high, the drone should throttle up. If their guess is just right, the drone should do a flip. The program should also include a print statement for when the user guesses a number that is not between 1-10 and a break if they want to quit the program. Finally, the drone should land.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Your final program should look something like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\nfrom CoDrone_mini import Direction\r\n\r\nimport time\r\n\r\nfrom random import randint\r\n\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\n\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\n\r\n\r\nthrottle = 20\r\n\r\nnumber = randint(1, 10)\u00a0 # randomly choose a number between 1-10\r\n\r\n\r\nwhile True:\r\n\r\n    guess = int(input(\"Guess a number from 1 - 10... or enter 0 to quit: \"))\u00a0 # get input from user\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 if guess == 0:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0    break\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 elif guess &gt; 10 or guess &lt; 0:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Number is not between 1-10. Try again.\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 elif guess == number:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Perfect!\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 time.sleep(0.05)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.flip(Direction.FORWARD)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 break\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 elif guess &lt; number:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Too low!\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_throttle(-throttle)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.move(1)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 elif guess &gt; number:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 print(\"Too High!\")\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.set_throttle(throttle)\r\n\r\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 drone.move(1)\r\n\r\ndrone.land()\r\n\r\ndrone.close()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbff20\" name=\"6a22149dbff20\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge 1: Magic 8 Ball<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The magic 8 Ball is a toy that had fluid inside it with a triangle that had different responses. To play, you would think of a question and then shake the ball. An answer to your question would appear in a window on the ball. To see an example of this, try out a Magic 8 Ball <a href=\"https:\/\/legomenon.com\/ask-magic-8-ball-game-online.html\">here<\/a>. <\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Now its time to turn your CoDrone Mini into a Magic 8 Ball!\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>For this program to work, the user will input a question. Your drone must then respond with an LED and flight movement. To complete this challenge, do the following:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create a user input for the question<\/li>\n<li>Create a function that randomly picks from a list of 4 or more predictions and returns the prediction<\/li>\n<li>Based on the return, have the drone LED light up a unique color and perform a unique flight movement<\/li>\n<li>Finally, print the result of the prediction (yes, no, possible, unlikely) for the user.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column][\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22149dbff92\" name=\"6a22149dbff92\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge 2: Random Flight<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this challenge, you will have your drone fly in 3 different random flight paths. To complete this challenge, do the following:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Choose the general steps your flight path will take and put them in a void function that takes two parameters, <em>move<\/em> and\u00a0<em>amount<\/em><\/li>\n<li>Call the function in a loop that executes 3 times<\/li>\n<li>For each loop iteration, generate a random number for each parameter and pass them in to the function call<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Once you have completed this program, your drone should fly the general route, but the distances and angles will be different.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Goals and Steps to Success [vc_column_text]Goals: By the end of this lesson, I will be able to: Describe how a computer generates random numbers Describe the range&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/3-5-random\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4145,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3473,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2125,2122,2134,2138],"class_list":["post-3761","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-python","lesson-tag-random","module-level-3","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3761","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":11,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3761\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":4500,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3761\/revisions\/4500"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4145"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3761"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3761"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3761"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}